{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"gh issue view 45 --repo mrkkucharski/vgt --json title,body,comments,labels,state && git status --short --branch && git log --oneline -8 && sed -n '1,220p' docs/GOAL.md && rg -n -i \\\"review|lalal|idempot|upload|minutes_left|preset|download\\\" . --glob '\"'!*.lock'\"'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"gh issue view 45 --repo mrkkucharski/vgt --json title,body,comments,labels,state && git status --short --branch && git log --oneline -8 && sed -n '1,220p' docs/GOAL.md && rg -n -i \\\"review|lalal|idempot|upload|minutes_left|preset|download\\\" . --glob '\"'!*.lock'\"'\"","aggregated_output":"{\"body\":\"Implement the only network-touching piece: the LALAL.AI **API v1** backend behind the `Separator` seam. See **[docs/stem-separation-plan.md](../blob/main/docs/stem-separation-plan.md)** — sub-issue **B**, §1 (API v1), and Acceptance criteria (§5).\\n\\n**Depends on #43 (operation model + seam) and #44 (final paths).** Do not start until both are closed.\\n\\n## Scope — v1 endpoints\\n- Auth header `X-License-Key` from **`LALAL_LICENSE_KEY`**, never persisted or logged. (v0 `Authorization: license …` is deprecated — not used.)\\n- `POST /api/v1/upload/` → `POST /api/v1/split/stem_separator/` → poll `POST /api/v1/check/` (task_ids) → download; plus `/api/v1/limits/minutes_left/`, `/api/v1/cancel/`, `/api/v1/delete/`.\\n- **Do not** use `/api/v1/split/multistem/` — per-stem-minute billing gives no saving and one-task-many-outputs would break per-operation resume (see plan §1).\\n- Presets: `splitter` (default `auto`), `dereverb_enabled`, `extraction_level`, fixed `encoder_format=\\\"wav\\\"`. (There is **no** `enhanced_processing_enabled` in v1.)\\n\\n## Recipe (five paid operations, each reference stem from the ORIGINAL)\\nupload original → vocals [keep stem + instrumental] → bass/drums/guitar from original [keep stems] → upload instrumental → guitar [keep back = `backing`]. The final guitar op is the **only** cascade.\\n\\n## Must-have durability\\n- Generate + persist a UUID **`idempotency_key`** before submission; persist task id immediately on success; on restart resume a known task. Ambiguous submission whose task identity can't be recovered **fails closed** (no auto-retry, no second charge).\\n- Pre-flight `minutes_left` vs sum of outstanding operation durations (vocal pair counts once); a run that can't cover the outstanding recipe starts **no** new paid tasks.\\n- Poll < 30 req/min with bounded backoff; handle `429`, task errors, cancellation, upload/task expiry, expired download URLs; re-upload only expired sources.\\n- Stream downloads to `.part`, validate length + readable WAV metadata/plausible duration, atomic rename, store SHA-256/size/duration. Partial files never treated as cached. Record requested **and** effective presets (incl. the model `auto` chose; pin it on a reconstruction retry).\\n\\n## Tests\\n- Mock v1 HTTP fixtures in CI (**no live calls**); assert `X-License-Key` redacted from exceptions/progress/sidecars/snapshots. One explicitly manual, opt-in smoke test for an account owner before release.\",\"comments\":[{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOTcQqas8AAAABK2DIWg\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mrkkucharski\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Dependency check: #43 is closed, but #44 is still open. Per this issue’s explicit instruction not to start until both dependencies are closed, no implementation work has been started. I am leaving the status unchanged; this is dependency ordering, not a human/external blocker.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-07-20T13:22:36Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mrkkucharski/vgt/issues/45#issuecomment-5022730330\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOTcQqas8AAAABK2jhnQ\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mrkkucharski\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Implemented and pushed LALAL API v1 backend (commits 68ceb76, 28794f7). Includes v1 upload/split/check/limits/cancel/delete, durable source/task/idempotency checkpoints with fail-closed ambiguity handling, bounded polling and WAV download validation, effective-model pinning, mocked HTTP tests, and an opt-in manual smoke-test procedure. Verified: 55 backend/project tests and 19 analysis tests pass (3 pre-existing Python deprecation warnings).\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-07-20T14:16:25Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mrkkucharski/vgt/issues/45#issuecomment-5023261085\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOTcQqas8AAAABK2onrA\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mrkkucharski\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Fix cycle 1 complete: source-upload reuse is now durable and scoped by content hash, so the four original-source operations share one LALAL upload while the instrumental cascade uploads separately. Task/idempotency state remains operation-local. Added regression coverage; ============================= test session starts ==============================\\nplatform darwin -- Python 3.11.15, pytest-9.1.1, pluggy-1.6.0\\nrootdir: /Users/marekkucharski/projects/.pm-worktrees/vgt/issue-45\\nconfigfile: pyproject.toml\\nplugins: anyio-4.14.2\\ncollected 27 items\\n\\ntests/test_lalal.py .....                                                [ 18%]\\ntests/test_separation.py ......................                          [100%]\\n\\n============================== 27 passed in 0.64s ============================== passes (27 tests). Pushed commit b8b5d08.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-07-20T14:24:47Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mrkkucharski/vgt/issues/45#issuecomment-5023344556\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true}],\"labels\":[{\"id\":\"LA_kwDOTcQqas8AAAACsQEnfA\",\"name\":\"status:working\",\"description\":\"\",\"color\":\"1d76db\"},{\"id\":\"LA_kwDOTcQqas8AAAACsQEoHw\",\"name\":\"implementer:codex\",\"description\":\"\",\"color\":\"0052cc\"},{\"id\":\"LA_kwDOTcQqas8AAAACsQEoaQ\",\"name\":\"reviewer:codex\",\"description\":\"\",\"color\":\"006b75\"},{\"id\":\"LA_kwDOTcQqas8AAAACsQEo6Q\",\"name\":\"priority:medium\",\"description\":\"\",\"color\":\"fbca04\"},{\"id\":\"LA_kwDOTcQqas8AAAACsSEeMw\",\"name\":\"fix-count:2\",\"description\":\"\",\"color\":\"e4e669\"}],\"state\":\"OPEN\",\"title\":\"M1-B: LALAL API v1 backend (LalalSeparator)\"}\n## issue-45-m1-b-lalal-api-v1-backend-lalalseparator...origin/main [ahead 3, behind 13]\nb8b5d08 fix(separation): reuse LALAL source uploads\n28794f7 fix(separation): pin effective LALAL auto model\n68ceb76 feat(separation): add LALAL API v1 backend\n158daee chore(pm): start fix issue #44 (codex)\n3565ce2 chore(pm): start review issue #44 (codex)\nc5ac3d5 chore(pm): start review issue #44 (claude)\n8354f94 chore(pm): start issue #44 (claude)\nf73839d chore(pm): start issue #44 (claude)\n# Goal\n\n## Background\nWe are building a (to some extent still experimental) virtual guitar teacher. We are at the initial phase.\nThe user interacts with vgt either from the command line or from the REAPER desktop app.\n\nIn REAPER the user has typically one original song; in the future there is a possibility of having more than\none. That song may have adjusted pitch, be normalized, or have some marks — but otherwise it is not expected to\nhave significant modifications. This is the **reference song**.\n\nThe student works on separate tracks — typically split into several stems:\na) vocals\nb) drums\nc) bass\nd) guitar(s)\ne) rest of the instruments\n\nFor practicing, the student may want to mute the original track, change play speed (preserving pitch), adjust\nthe volume of specific parts (e.g. volume up on bass and drums, volume down on guitar) etc. — so they can play\nalong with specific track sets. And so on.\n\nThe whole initiative is divided into sub-projects or phases. Each phase builds an incremental piece of the\nfunctionality.\n\n## Phases\n\nThe initiative is built in incremental phases. Each adds a self-contained slice and builds on the `[vgt]`\nconventions and the `<project>.vgt` sidecar established by the phases before it. \"Done\" for the whole project is\nthe union of every phase's deliverables below.\n\n### Phase 0 — REAPER-plumbing foundation *(delivered)*\n\nEstablishes how vgt locates, opens, and safely augments a REAPER project, and where vgt stores its own state.\nShipped:\n- **locating a REAPER project** — accept a project path as input;\n- **defaulting to the current project** — when no project is given and there is already a REAPER project in the\n  working directory, assume the user wants to work with that one;\n- **opening the project and reading relevant information** — parse the project and read at least: sample rate,\n  tempo/time-signature, and the existing track list (names and GUIDs) so vgt can tell which tracks are already\n  vgt-managed;\n- **storing vgt settings next to the REAPER project** — a single sidecar file living alongside the\n  `.RPP` and sharing its name with a `.vgt` extension (e.g. `Reaper Project.RPP` → `Reaper Project.vgt`), holding\n  vgt's own state (schema version, the vgt-managed track GUIDs it created, and any config);\n- **preparing a \"vgt managed\" area for practice tracks** — a REAPER track folder (and a `[vgt]` name prefix on\n  every track/region vgt creates) so a student can immediately identify what vgt owns;\n- **choosing a reference track and mirroring it** — the apply action asks which of the project's own tracks is\n  the reference, names the managed folder after it (`[vgt] <reference track name>`), and mirrors that one track's\n  media into the managed area.\n\n### Phase 1 — Reference analysis *(delivered)*\n\nAnalyze the chosen reference track — **the full mix; no stem separation yet** — and record what vgt learns about\nthe song, both in the sidecar and as `[vgt]`-owned objects in the project. From the reference audio, detect:\n- **tempo & beat grid** — BPM, downbeat offset, and time signature;\n- **key** — root + scale (major/minor);\n- **sections** — intro / verse / chorus / … boundaries;\n- **chords** — beat-aligned chord labels (maj/min vocabulary).\n\nPhase 1 delivers:\n- **an analysis stage in the CLI** — heavy analysis runs in the Python CLI, never inside REAPER; the ReaScript\n  action passes the reference track's source-file path (already identified in phase 0) to the CLI;\n- **persisting analysis in the sidecar** — extend the `<project>.vgt` schema (bump `schema_version`) to hold the\n  detected tempo/key/sections/chords alongside phase 0's state;\n- **reflecting analysis into the project**, additively and idempotently, as `[vgt]`-owned objects:\n  - a **tempo map** — subject to the tempo-map rule: written only when the project still has a single default\n    tempo marker; otherwise left untouched and offered non-invasively (an unmuted `[vgt]` beat-marker track). A\n    re-apply refreshes a vgt-created map with newly detected/corrected tempo data as long as the live map is\n    still demonstrably the one vgt wrote (a fingerprint recorded in the sidecar proves it); the moment a human\n    edits it by hand, vgt never touches it again and falls back to the non-invasive beat-marker track instead;\n  - `[vgt]` **section regions** (intro/verse/chorus/…), renamable and movable by the user;\n  - a **muted `[vgt] Chords`** track carrying the beat-aligned chord labels as text items, editable on the\n    timeline;\n  - a single **`vgt sync`** action reads both the edited chord items and the edited section regions back into\n    the sidecar as human-verified corrections in one invocation, without disturbing the machine-detected values\n    each stage keeps alongside them (see README's \"Correcting chords and sections in REAPER\").\n\n**Phase 1 was the analysis slice** of the [phase1-song-prep-plan.md](phase1-song-prep-plan.md) roadmap.\nStem separation — deferred out of phase 1 — is now **Phase 2** (below). Guitar MIDI reference generation,\npractice controls (stem muting / looping / tempo-ramp), and performance scoring remain deferred to later phases.\n\n### Phase 2 — Stem separation *(current)*\n\nSeparate the reference track into practice stems using **LALAL.AI as the sole backend** — offline separation\n(Demucs/UVR/RoFormer) is explicitly deferred. Reproducing the user's proven manual workflow, vgt produces six\nartifacts via five paid split operations, isolating each **reference** stem from the **original** mix (with one\ndeliberate cascade for the guitarless practice bed) and loading them as `[vgt]` tracks. The full design — LALAL\nAPI v1 contract, the fixed recipe, durability / no-double-charge invariants, artifact layout, and acceptance\ncriteria — is in [stem-separation-plan.md](stem-separation-plan.md). Phase 2 delivers:\n- **six stems** — `vocals`, `instrumental` (mix − vocals), `bass`, `drums`, `guitar` (electric/acoustic,\n  user-declared), and `backing (no guitar)`;\n- **a LALAL v1 backend** behind a thin `Separator` seam, authenticated only by the `LALAL_LICENSE_KEY`\n  environment variable (never persisted or logged), with idempotency-keyed, durably-checkpointed operations so\n  paid work is never repeated or double-charged;\n- **a `stems` block in the sidecar** — per-operation and per-artifact provenance, content-hash cache identity,\n  and a stable per-project artifact namespace under a `vgt/` subfolder next to the RPP;\n- **six `[vgt]` stem tracks** imported additively and idempotently with project-relative media paths;\n- **cost-safe CLI semantics** — ordinary `vgt analyze --force` never spends credits; repeating paid work\n  requires an explicit `--force-stems` with a cost preview and confirmation.\n\n**Out of scope for phase 2** (deferred to later phases): offline separation (UVR / RoFormer / Demucs), guitar\nMIDI reference generation, practice controls (stem muting / looping / tempo-ramp), and performance scoring.\n\n## Requirements\n\n- **Non-destructive.** Never overwrite, rename, delete, or modify any track or object vgt did not create.\n  Everything vgt creates carries the `[vgt]` prefix; only `[vgt]`-owned objects are ever touched. A re-apply\n  first removes only its own `[vgt]` objects before recreating them.\n- **Respect REAPER settings.** Open and read the REAPER project (and relevant preferences) and honor them —\n  do not fight the project's existing sample rate, tempo, etc.\n- **Prefer live, in-app manipulation.** The intended mechanism is to manipulate the project through the REAPER\n  API via a ReaScript action (not by editing `.RPP` text), so the modifications appear immediately in the user's\n  open project and REAPER handles project construction correctly. Where a piece is not yet technically feasible\n  in-app, note it explicitly rather than silently falling back to text edits.\n- **Analysis stays out of the DAW process.** ML/DSP analysis runs in the Python CLI; REAPER only reads the\n  reference source path and applies results through the API. The DAW never loads heavy analysis dependencies.\n- **Correctable.** Auto-analysis will sometimes be wrong; every detected value (tempo, key, sections, chords) is\n  overridable, and corrections survive re-runs of the analysis.\n- **CLI-initiated.** A command-line interface initiates the actions, with the intent that it be invoked from a\n  ReaScript action inside REAPER. The ReaScript wrapper is a thin caller; the CLI does the work.\n- **Idempotent.** Running the same command twice produces the same result — no duplicate tracks, folders, regions,\n  or settings. Re-running reconciles vgt's managed area to the intended state.\n- **Documented.** There is documentation describing how vgt works and how to run it.\n./src/vgt/separation.py:8:every recipe/cache/partial-resume/sidecar code path that the real LALAL\n./src/vgt/separation.py:172:    effective_presets: dict[str, Any] = field(default_factory=dict)\n./src/vgt/separation.py:213:      - \"before_submit\"      -- before anything happens (e.g. upload never went out)\n./src/vgt/separation.py:218:      - \"before_download:<side>\" -- before writing that side's audio at all\n./src/vgt/separation.py:219:      - \"after_download:<side>\"  -- after the `.part` file exists but before\n./src/vgt/separation.py:250:        idempotency_key = resume_state.get(\"idempotency_key\") or str(uuid.uuid4())\n./src/vgt/separation.py:254:            task_id = f\"fake-task-{idempotency_key}\"\n./src/vgt/separation.py:255:            checkpoint({\"idempotency_key\": idempotency_key, \"task_id\": task_id, \"status\": \"submitted\"})\n./src/vgt/separation.py:258:            checkpoint({\"idempotency_key\": idempotency_key, \"task_id\": task_id, \"status\": \"resumed\"})\n./src/vgt/separation.py:263:            self._maybe_fail(f\"before_download:{side}\")\n./src/vgt/separation.py:267:            self._maybe_fail(f\"after_download:{side}\")\n./src/vgt/separation.py:271:        checkpoint({\"idempotency_key\": idempotency_key, \"task_id\": task_id, \"status\": \"completed\"})\n./src/vgt/separation.py:274:            backend_state={\"idempotency_key\": idempotency_key, \"task_id\": task_id, \"status\": \"completed\"},\n./src/vgt/separation.py:275:            effective_presets={\"splitter\": \"Andromeda\" if spec.splitter == \"auto\" else spec.splitter},\n./src/vgt/separation.py:353:        \"requested_presets\": op_def.spec.to_dict(),\n./src/vgt/separation.py:354:        \"effective_presets\": {},\n./src/vgt/separation.py:397:    \"\"\"Return a reusable remote-upload identity for these exact source bytes.\n./src/vgt/separation.py:399:    LALAL uploads are independent of a split task.  The four original-source\n./src/vgt/separation.py:400:    operations must therefore share one upload rather than uploading the same\n./src/vgt/separation.py:401:    original four times.  Upload metadata lives in per-operation opaque state\n./src/vgt/separation.py:403:    only the source identity, never an operation's idempotency key or task id.\n./src/vgt/separation.py:405:    and will replace only that source upload when needed.\n./src/vgt/separation.py:455:    # A fresh operation against bytes another operation already upl