ript.py::test_read_chords_writes_corrected_segments_as_human_verified` and `tests/test_analysis.py::test_key_and_chord_corrections_survive_rerun` assert the correction survives re-analysis.\", \"- [x] Non-destructive/idempotent invariants \\u2014 re-apply only touches GUIDs it recorded and matches by current `[vgt]` name (`remove_previous_managed_tracks`), and both the phase-0 and phase-1 live verifiers explicitly check for no duplicate tracks/regions on a second pass.\", \"- [x] Documentation of install/apply/analyze/chord-correction workflow \\u2014 `README.md` has dedicated sections for all four (`## Install and inspect`, `## Apply inside REAPER`, `## Analyze the reference track (Phase 1)`, `## Correcting chords in REAPER`).\"], \"test_evidence\": [\"- `uv run pytest tests -q` \\u2014 **could not execute**: this session's sandbox only allowlists `git add/commit/push` and `gh repo/issue/label` Bash commands (`.claude/settings.local.json`); any `uv`, `python3 -m pytest`, or even `python3 -c` invocation was rejected with \\\"This command requires approval\\\" and no interactive approver was available. I could not independently re-run the suite.\", \"- Historical, self-reported evidence in commit/issue history stands in for direct execution: issue #11 comment records `uv run pytest -q` \\u2192 \\\"23 passed\\\" plus a disposable-copy live REAPER run (`scripts/verify_phase1_apply.py --run-live`) covering default-tempo-map, existing-tempo-map fallback, and idempotence; commit `0cf9ad9` (issue #17, chords) states \\\"Verified live against REAPER: edit \\u2192 read-chords \\u2192 corrected sidecar \\u2192 re-apply repaints identically (idempotent), and vgt analyze leaves the corrected stage alone.\\\"\", \"- Static review of `tests/test_analysis.py`, `test_chords.py`, `test_tempo.py`, `test_sections.py`, `test_project.py`, `test_reascript.py` (36 test functions total) shows coverage for all four Phase 1 detectors, sidecar schema upgrade, correction-survives-rerun for tempo/key/sections/chords, idempotent apply, non-destructive scope, and the chord read-back round-trip \\u2014 no gaps found by inspection.\"], \"status_evidence\": [\"- `gh issue list --repo mrkkucharski/vgt --state closed` \\u2014 all 10 issues closed (declare-verification-command, phase 0 plumbing, live-verify phase 0, phase 1 umbrella + 4 detector sub-issues, phase 1 apply, chord editing/read-back); none open, no `status:blocked`/`status:needs-fix` remaining.\", \"- `docs/phase0-live-verification.md:64` still says the recorded run is \\\"_Pending re-run after the reference-track-selection change_\\\" \\u2014 a stale doc note; superseded in practice by the later live runs recorded in the issue #11 and #17 commit/comment history, but the doc itself was never refreshed. Minor documentation-accuracy gap, not a functional gap.\", \"- The project's declared `verification_command` (per `.pm/log.ndjson`) is `git diff --check`, a whitespace/diff-hygiene check only \\u2014 it does not itself execute the test suite. Actual functional verification depended on the implementer/reviewer agents manually running `pytest`/the live-REAPER scripts each cycle, as recorded in issue comments.\", \"- `docs/GOAL.md` \\\"Out of scope for phase 1\\\" items (stem separation, guitar MIDI, practice controls, scoring) are correctly absent from the codebase \\u2014 no premature scope creep found.\"], \"reason\": \"Every Phase 0 and Phase 1 deliverable in `docs/GOAL.md` has a corresponding, non-stubbed implementation (`src/vgt/*.py`, `reascript/vgt_initialize.lua`, `reascript/vgt_read_chords.lua`), a matching CLI surface, and test coverage in `tests/`. I was blocked from directly re-running the test suite by this session's command allowlist, but the development history (commit messages and issue comments across issues #4, #8-#11, #17) documents concrete, non-fabricated evidence of both a green pytest run and a disposable-copy live-REAPER run at each key merge, including the most recent one (chord 