{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'for n in 46 47 48 49 50 51; do gh issue view \"$n\" --repo mrkkucharski/vgt --json number,title,state,body,comments,labels 2>/dev/null; done'","aggregated_output":"{\"body\":\"Wire separation into the CLI with cost-safe, partial-success semantics. See **[docs/stem-separation-plan.md](../blob/main/docs/stem-separation-plan.md)** — sub-issue **C**.\\n\\n**Depends on #45 (LALAL backend).** Do not start until #45 is closed.\\n\\n## Scope\\n- Fold separation into `vgt analyze` as the **last** stage, progress on stderr. Refactor persistence so each successful local stage and each separation checkpoint is atomically written immediately. If LALAL is unavailable, local tempo/key/sections/chords results remain saved; report the stems error and **exit nonzero** after describing the partial success.\\n- `--force` refreshes only **non-paid local** analysis and **never re-bills** cached stems. Repeating paid work requires **`--force-stems`** + an exact operation/cost preview + interactive confirmation; non-interactive automation must also pass an explicit acknowledgment flag.\\n- Recipe/artifact set stay fixed; `--guitar electric|acoustic` is the only song-level choice (follows #43's persistence rules). Before spending: print remaining minutes, estimated operation cost, and **cached vs outstanding operations** (not merely artifact count).\\n- `vgt status`: report the five operations + six artifacts, requested/effective splitter + guitar type, remote/in-progress/error state, local file validity, and quality-verification status — **without** exposing credentials or making network calls.\\n\\n## Acceptance\\n- `vgt analyze --force` submits **zero** cached split operations. `--force-stems` cannot spend without cost disclosure + explicit consent. Status distinguishes cached/outstanding/in-progress/failed/missing/corrupt/human-verified.\",\"comments\":[{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOTcQqas8AAAABK2rZXA\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mrkkucharski\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Blocked pending closure of #45 (LALAL API v1 backend), which this issue explicitly depends on. No implementation started.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-07-20T14:29:15Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mrkkucharski/vgt/issues/46#issuecomment-5023390044\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true}],\"labels\":[{\"id\":\"LA_kwDOTcQqas8AAAACsQEnlA\",\"name\":\"status:blocked\",\"description\":\"\",\"color\":\"d93f0b\"},{\"id\":\"LA_kwDOTcQqas8AAAACsQEoHw\",\"name\":\"implementer:codex\",\"description\":\"\",\"color\":\"0052cc\"},{\"id\":\"LA_kwDOTcQqas8AAAACsQEo6Q\",\"name\":\"priority:medium\",\"description\":\"\",\"color\":\"fbca04\"}],\"number\":46,\"state\":\"OPEN\",\"title\":\"M1-C: CLI wiring + partial-success semantics for stem separation\"}\n{\"body\":\"Import the separated stems as `[vgt]` tracks in the open REAPER project. See **[docs/stem-separation-plan.md](../blob/main/docs/stem-separation-plan.md)** — sub-issue **D**.\\n\\n**Depends on #43 (sidecar contract), #44 (paths/namespace), #45 (stem outputs exist).** Do not start until all three are closed.\\n\\n## Scope\\n- Extend `vgt_initialize.lua`: after the mirror, read `analysis.stems.artifacts` and create six `[vgt]` stem tracks — `[vgt] Vocals`, `[vgt] Instrumental`, `[vgt] Bass`, `[vgt] Drums`, `[vgt] Guitar`, `[vgt] Backing (no guitar)` — **time-based** positioning, offset-shifted, GUIDs tracked in `managed_track_guids`, **idempotent** on re-apply (same discipline as existing `[vgt]` tracks).\\n- Resolve files only through the sidecar-recorded artifact namespace; missing/invalid artifacts are **skipped with a clear warning**.\\n- Insert WAVs as time-based media and **verify in a saved real RPP** that REAPER serializes **project-relative** paths (supplying a local file to the API is not proof of serialization).\\n- Concurrency: honor the `stems.in_progress` lease — the ReaScript refuses to apply while a live separation lease is present (see plan §2 concurrency protocol); it writes only ReaScript-owned fields.\\n\\n## Acceptance\\n- A saved-project test proves six stem tracks are offset-shifted, time-based, project-relative, `[vgt]`-owned, idempotent on re-apply; user tracks and regions remain untouched.\",\"comments\":[],\"labels\":[{\"id\":\"LA_kwDOTcQqas8AAAACsQEnRA\",\"name\":\"status:queued\",\"description\":\"\",\"color\":\"ededed\"},{\"id\":\"LA_kwDOTcQqas8AAAACsQEo6Q\",\"name\":\"priority:medium\",\"description\":\"\",\"color\":\"fbca04\"}],\"number\":47,\"state\":\"OPEN\",\"title\":\"M1-D: ReaScript import of stem tracks into the project\"}\n{\"body\":\"Listening evaluation of the real LALAL output. See **[docs/stem-separation-plan.md](../blob/main/docs/stem-separation-plan.md)** — sub-issue **F**.\\n\\n**Depends on #45 (real stems) and #47 (imported in REAPER).** Do not start until both are closed.\\n\\n## Scope\\n- On the golden songs, listen for **interference and damage** in the LALAL guitar and backing stems (residual vocals, warble, lost transients).\\n- Note electric-vs-acoustic, the **effective splitter** (`auto` selection), and `extraction_level` (`deep_extraction` vs `clear_cut`) quality in a findings doc.\\n- Feeds the deferred M7 golden-song evaluation; the decisive test is whether a stem works for practice, not a numeric metric.\",\"comments\":[],\"labels\":[{\"id\":\"LA_kwDOTcQqas8AAAACsQEnRA\",\"name\":\"status:queued\",\"description\":\"\",\"color\":\"ededed\"},{\"id\":\"LA_kwDOTcQqas8AAAACsQEovA\",\"name\":\"priority:low\",\"description\":\"\",\"color\":\"9be9a8\"}],\"number\":48,\"state\":\"OPEN\",\"title\":\"M1-F: Stem-separation evaluation pass on golden songs\"}\n{\"body\":\"Closes #43\\n\\n## Changes\\n\\nSee issue #43 for details.\",\"comments\":[],\"labels\":[],\"number\":49,\"state\":\"MERGED\",\"title\":\"M1-A: Operation model + Separator seam + fake backend (stem separation)\"}\n{\"body\":\"Closes #44\\n\\n## Changes\\n\\nSee issue #44 for details.\",\"comments\":[],\"labels\":[],\"number\":50,\"state\":\"MERGED\",\"title\":\"M1-E: Consolidate vgt artifacts under a vgt/ subfolder namespace\"}\n{\"body\":\"Closes #45\\n\\n## Changes\\n\\nSee issue #45 for details.\",\"comments\":[],\"labels\":[],\"number\":51,\"state\":\"OPEN\",\"title\":\"M1-B: LALAL API v1 backend (LalalSeparator)\"}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
